Vita (--vita-fast-draw-runs=off|on|verify, platform/vita/runtime/fast_painter.hpp): draws that
follow each other with nothing changed between them are sent as one. The game draws snow, rain,
twilight squares, cloud shadows and text one quad per draw command; a Vita3K census of 12 Nov
counted 2,498 such draws of 3,016 per frame in the Palace of Twilight and 2,029 of 2,524 in
Snowpeak Ruins, each costing the GX worker a whole draw. When a quad or triangle-list draw is
read, the commands after it are looked at: unchanged register writes and NOPs are passed over,
and every following draw of the same primitive and vertex format joins it (up to 1,020
vertices). The look stops at the first other command, so no state can change inside a run. Only
direct-attribute vertex descriptors are taken, so static display lists and the geometry cache
are not involved. Verify joins nothing and checks, at each draw that would have joined, that
Aurora's own change flags say nothing changed. Off by default.

--- a/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
